course: dictionary
lesson: 4962
title: The inch: a small unit of length
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inch is a small unit of length, about as wide as your thumb. You use inches to measure short things, like a pencil or a phone screen. Twelve inches make one foot, and 36 inches make one yard.
explain: The word inch has a second meaning too. «The snail began to inch across the wet path» means it moved very slowly, a little bit at a time. You can tell from the words around it: a snail does not run, so inch must mean slow movement.
explain: «Every inch» means all of something. If the garden was searched every inch, then no part of it was left out. Look at the clues around a word to find which meaning fits.
fact: One inch is about as wide as your thumb.
fact: 12 inches make 1 foot.
fact: 3 feet make 1 yard, so 1 yard is 36 inches.
fact: To inch forward means to move very slowly, a little bit at a time.
fact: «Every inch» means all of something, with nothing left out.
exercise: «One yard is 3 feet, and one foot is 12 inches.» How many inches are in one foot? | 36 | 3 | 1 | *12
exercise: «The snail began to inch across the wet path.» What does inch mean here? | To measure the path | To run fast | *To move very slowly, a little bit at a time | To jump high
exercise: «She searched every inch of the garden.» What does every inch mean? | Only the edge of the garden | A tiny part, one inch wide | Only the flowers | *All of the garden, with nothing left out
test: An inch is about as wide as your what? | Hand | *Thumb | Foot | Nose
test: «Adult belts are made for adult bodies, so a child uses a booster seat until the belt fits, usually until about 145 to 150 cm (4 feet 9 inches) tall.» How many inches is 4 feet 9 inches? | 60 | *57 | 12 | 45
exam: «Then she shrinks to ten inches and grows to over nine feet.» How many inches make one yard? | 24 | *36 | 48 | 12
